data: {"text":"1. That the Applicant apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 215/2026 dated 10.04.2026, registered at PS Gandhi Maidan, under"}

data: {"text":" Sections 318(4) and 336(3) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. The Applicant has"}

data: {"text":" not been arrested yet but apprehends imminent arrest in the said case.\n\n2. That the Applicant app"}

data: {"text":"rehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 215/2026 dated 10.04.2026 lodged at PS Gandhi Maidan, Patna. The FIR has been lodged on the basis of a false complaint by the de-"}

data: {"text":"facto complainant arising out of a business dispute between the parties.\n\n3. That the Applicant is a businessman of standing in the community and has deep"}

data: {"text":" roots in the locality. The Applicant has no criminal antecedents and has always been a law"}

data: {"text":"-abiding citizen who has conducted his business activities in accordance with law.\n\n4. That the Applicant undertakes to cooperate fully with the investigation and shall"}

data: {"text":" not leave the territorial jurisdiction of the State of Bihar without prior permission of this Hon'ble Court. The Applicant is ready and willing to join the investigation as"}

data: {"text":" and when required by the investigating agency.\n\n5. That the allegations levelled against the Applicant are completely false and"}

data: {"text":" baseless. The Applicant has been falsely implicated in the present case due to malicious intentions"}

data: {"text":" of the de-facto complainant who wants to pressurize the Applicant in connection with their ongoing"}

data: {"text":" business dispute.\n\n6. That the matter in question is essentially a civil dispute arising out of business transactions"}

data: {"text":" between the parties, which has been given a criminal colour by the de-facto complainant with"}

data: {"text":" ulterior motives. The complainant is trying to use the criminal law as a tool to settle"}

data: {"text":" scores in what is essentially a commercial disagreement.\n\n7. That the Applicant subm"}

data: {"text":"its that the right to personal liberty is a fundamental right guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India,"}

data: {"text":" and the same cannot be curtailed without following due"}

data: {"text":" process of law. The custodial interrogation of the Applicant is not necessary as the Applicant is willing to cooperate with the investigation voluntarily.\n\n8. That the Hon'ble Supreme"}

data: {"text":" Court in Sushila Aggarwal v. State (2020) 5 SCC 1 has laid down the conditions for granting anticipatory bail,"}

data: {"text":" which include the nature and gravity of the accusation, the antecedents of the applicant, the possibility of the applicant fle"}

data: {"text":"eing from justice, and the likelihood of the accusation being true.\n\n9. That the Applicant has strong roots"}

data: {"text":" in the community and is a respectable businessman who has been residing at the same address for years"}

data: {"text":". There is no possibility of the Applicant fleeing from justice or tampering with evidence,"}

data: {"text":" as the Applicant is ready to abide by any conditions that this Hon'ble Court may"}

data: {"text":" deem fit to impose.\n\n10. That the offences under Sections 318(4) and 336(3) of BNS,"}

data: {"text":" 2023 are non-bailable in nature, and hence the Applicant is constrained to approach this Hon'ble Court for anticipatory bail to"}

data: {"text":" protect himself from unnecessary harassment and detention.\n\n11. That the investigation is pending"}

data: {"text":" and the Applicant apprehends that he may be arrested any time by the investigating agency. The Applicant subm"}

data: {"text":"its that his custodial interrogation would serve no useful purpose as he is ready"}

data: {"text":" to join the investigation voluntarily and provide all necessary cooperation.\n\n12. That the Applicant undertakes to abide by all conditions that"}

data: {"text":" may be imposed by this Hon'ble Court while granting anticipatory bail and shall not misuse the liberty"}

data: {"text":" granted to him. The Applicant has full faith in the judicial system and is confident that truth will ultimately"}

data: {"text":" prevail."}

event: template_sections
data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"cause_title","type":"template","content":"IN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT PATNA\nAT Patna\n\nCr. Misc. No. _____ of 2026\n\nIN THE MATTER OF:\n\nSuresh Prasad Singh\nS/o Late Shri Ramesh Prasad Singh\nAge: 45 years\nR/o Flat 4B, Boring Road, Patna, Bihar - 800001\n                                              ... Petitioner\n\nVersus\n\nState of Bihar through the Principal Secretary, Home Department, Government of Bihar, Patna\n                                              ... Respondent","alignment":"center"},{"section_id":"application_heading","type":"template","content":"APPLICATION FOR ANTICIPATORY BAIL UNDER SECTION 482 OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023","alignment":"center"},{"section_id":"addressing_clause","type":"template","content":"TO,\nTHE HONOURABLE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT PATNA,\nPatna\n\nMOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. That the Applicant apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 215/2026 dated 10.04.2026, registered at PS Gandhi Maidan, under Sections 318(4) and 336(3) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. The Applicant has not been arrested yet but apprehends imminent arrest in the said case.\n\n2. That the Applicant apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 215/2026 dated 10.04.2026 lodged at PS Gandhi Maidan, Patna. The FIR has been lodged on the basis of a false complaint by the de-facto complainant arising out of a business dispute between the parties.\n\n3. That the Applicant is a businessman of standing in the community and has deep roots in the locality. The Applicant has no criminal antecedents and has always been a law-abiding citizen who has conducted his business activities in accordance with law.\n\n4. That the Applicant undertakes to cooperate fully with the investigation and shall not leave the territorial jurisdiction of the State of Bihar without prior permission of this Hon'ble Court. The Applicant is ready and willing to join the investigation as and when required by the investigating agency.\n\n5. That the allegations levelled against the Applicant are completely false and baseless. The Applicant has been falsely implicated in the present case due to malicious intentions of the de-facto complainant who wants to pressurize the Applicant in connection with their ongoing business dispute.\n\n6. That the matter in question is essentially a civil dispute arising out of business transactions between the parties, which has been given a criminal colour by the de-facto complainant with ulterior motives. The complainant is trying to use the criminal law as a tool to settle scores in what is essentially a commercial disagreement.\n\n7. That the Applicant submits that the right to personal liberty is a fundamental right guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India, and the same cannot be curtailed without following due process of law. The custodial interrogation of the Applicant is not necessary as the Applicant is willing to cooperate with the investigation voluntarily.\n\n8. That the Hon'ble Supreme Court in Sushila Aggarwal v. State (2020) 5 SCC 1 has laid down the conditions for granting anticipatory bail, which include the nature and gravity of the accusation, the antecedents of the applicant, the possibility of the applicant fleeing from justice, and the likelihood of the accusation being true.\n\n9. That the Applicant has strong roots in the community and is a respectable businessman who has been residing at the same address for years. There is no possibility of the Applicant fleeing from justice or tampering with evidence, as the Applicant is ready to abide by any conditions that this Hon'ble Court may deem fit to impose.\n\n10. That the offences under Sections 318(4) and 336(3) of BNS, 2023 are non-bailable in nature, and hence the Applicant is constrained to approach this Hon'ble Court for anticipatory bail to protect himself from unnecessary harassment and detention.\n\n11. That the investigation is pending and the Applicant apprehends that he may be arrested any time by the investigating agency. The Applicant submits that his custodial interrogation would serve no useful purpose as he is ready to join the investigation voluntarily and provide all necessary cooperation.\n\n12. That the Applicant undertakes to abide by all conditions that may be imposed by this Hon'ble Court while granting anticipatory bail and shall not misuse the liberty granted to him. The Applicant has full faith in the judicial system and is confident that truth will ultimately prevail."},{"section_id":"prayer","type":"template","content":"PRAYER\n\nIt is, therefore, most humbly prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:\n\na) Grant Anticipatory Bail to the Petitioner, Suresh Prasad Singh, in the event of arrest in connection with FIR No. 215/2026 dated 10.04.2026, PS Gandhi Maidan, under Section 482 of BNSS, 2023, on such terms and conditions as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit;\n\nb) Direct that in the event of arrest, the Petitioner shall be released on bail forthwith;\n\nc) Pass such other orders as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances of the case, in the interest of justice.\n\nAnd for this act of kindness, the petitioner shall ever pray.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"verification","type":"template","content":"VERIFICATION\n\nI, Suresh Prasad Singh, the Petitioner herein above named, do hereby solemnly affirm and state that the contents of paragraphs 1 to 12 of the above petition are true and correct to the best of my knowledge and belief and nothing material has been concealed therefrom.\n\nVerified at Patna on this _____ day of _________, 2026.\n\nDEPONENT\n\n\n_________________________\nSuresh Prasad Singh\n(Petitioner)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"advocate_block","type":"template","content":"THROUGH:\n\n_________________________\nSmoke Test\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. ____________________\n\nPlace: Patna\nDate: 04 May 2026","alignment":"right"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

